WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.380
Interpreter architectures make a program and its
execution state explicit data managed by an engine.

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:11.612
This can support portability or simulate a machine
that is not directly available.

00:00:11.612 --> 00:00:17.098
A virtual machine is an abstraction, not a
requirement to interpret every instruction.

00:00:17.098 --> 00:00:23.415
Consider compilation, validation and build-time
dependencies when explaining the complete execution

00:00:23.415 --> 00:00:24.244
architecture.

00:00:24.244 --> 00:00:30.184
Process-control architecture separates the process,
measurements and control decisions.

00:00:30.184 --> 00:00:34.896
Identify the controlled variable, manipulated
variable and set point.

00:00:34.896 --> 00:00:40.085
Feedback uses observed results to adjust action;
open-loop control does not.

00:00:40.085 --> 00:00:46.913
Simple diagrams explain these relationships, but an
implemented controller must also address timing,

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:51.488
disturbances and limits before its behavior can be
judged reliable.

00:00:51.488 --> 00:00:54.669
Client–server describes roles in an interaction.

00:00:54.669 --> 00:01:00.898
Keeping query processing near data can reduce some
transfers, but network and failure behavior

00:01:00.898 --> 00:01:02.887
remain architectural concerns.

00:01:02.887 --> 00:01:06.134
Discovery, state and coordination affect scaling.

00:01:06.134 --> 00:01:12.429
A useful diagram explains who requests what and how
the interaction behaves when the service is

00:01:12.429 --> 00:01:15.743
slow, unavailable or returns an uncertain outcome.

00:01:15.788 --> 00:01:20.632
Peer-to-peer systems let participants share both
client and server roles.

00:01:20.632 --> 00:01:26.738
BitTorrent gains capacity from exchanging pieces
during download, not only after completion.

00:01:26.738 --> 00:01:31.980
Check discovery and bootstrap mechanisms before
claiming full decentralization.

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:38.484
Resilience, privacy and scaling depend on the
protocol and peer behavior, including partitions and

00:01:38.484 --> 00:01:41.271
unavailable or untrustworthy participants.

00:01:41.271 --> 00:01:46.580
Keep the model boundary explicit and connect each
conclusion to its assumptions.
